  "notes": "One of the most common formal verbs in Japanese. Appears constantly in news, official announcements, and business documents. Often used in passive form {実施|じっし}される.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {調査|ちょうさ}を{実施|じっし}する: to conduct a survey/investigation\n- {訓練|くんれん}を{実施|じっし}する: to carry out training\n- {計画|けいかく}を{実施|じっし}する: to execute a plan\n- {実施|じっし}{日|び}: implementation date\n- {実施|じっし}{要項|ようこう}: implementation guidelines\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {行|おこな}う: to carry out, to conduct — slightly less formal, also very common\n- {施行|しこう}する: to enforce (a law) — specifically for putting laws into effect\n- {実行|じっこう}する: to execute, to carry out — emphasizes actually doing it, can be used for personal actions too",
